{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170797-what-are-the-iconic-solar-effects","id":1170797,"title":"What are the iconic Solar effects?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-26T16:16:02-08:00","id":1170797,"title":"What are the iconic Solar effects?","content":"In the thread <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset\">If you could change the Solar Charmset</a>, there's a lot of interesting discussion on what kinds of alterations people would like to do to the Solar Charmset. The purpose of the thread is to streamline the set for inclusion in a homebrew setting that still uses the Exalted 3e mechanical engine (at least I <i>think</i> so?).<br /> <br /> However, I think the opposite question is also interesting. If you were to try to recreate the Solar Exalted in another setting, or in another system, or just trying to get to the core of their themes, what effects do you think need to be there? This could be individual Charms, or an effect that several Charms create together. It could also be something covered by Backgrounds or Merits, like the propensity to recover their rightful Artifacts from their previous incarnations' graves.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, I personally think that some kind of perfect defense (Heavenly Guardian Defense), some kind of unarmed knockback effect (Heaven Thunder Hammer), Craftsman Needs No Tools, Worshipful Lackey Acquisition and Tiger-Warrior Training Technique are important aspects of the Solar idea and need to have some sort of representation in any translation of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T17:24:59-08:00","id":1170812,"title":"","content":"Eye of the unconquered sun is pretty iconic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T18:09:05-08:00","id":1170819,"title":"","content":"Heaven Thunder Hammer, Heavenly Guardian Defense, Wyld Shaping Technique, Solar Circle Sorcery, Hypnotic Tongue Technique, Phantom-Conjuring Performance, Memory-Reweaving Discipline","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T20:17:48-08:00","id":1170844,"title":"","content":"Everything and nothing at all. The iconic solar trait is their adaptability and excellence in every thing they touch. As opposed to other exalts who have very specific themes and in those can even surpass solars, the solars are just good at everything, leaving them without obvious exploitable weaknesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T20:44:05-08:00","id":1170848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170797-what-are-the-iconic-solar-effects?p=1170844#post1170844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything and nothing at all. The iconic solar trait is their adaptability and excellence in every thing they touch. As opposed to other exalts who have very specific themes and in those can even surpass solars, the solars are just good at everything, leaving them without obvious exploitable weaknesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think adaptability is particularly Solar. They're not bad at being adaptable, but Lunars are the masters of adaptation.<br /> <br /> I'd say that Solars are the best at a finite range of skills, at which they shine brighter than any other. Which skills those are vary from Solar to Solar, but probably some two to five Abilities would become a particular Solar's domain of excellence. <br /> <br /> Layer that specific excellence with some supernatural toughness. Add a bit of holy might against beings of darkness. Add a bit of predestiny and divine authority, and you have a Solar.<br /> <br /> <br /> To make a Solar-ish in another system...<br /> <br /> I think I could do something (in my mind) similar in World of Darkness, using the Arete rules in Mirrors, with a small number of Simple Charms brought forward. Sunder's list is pretty good, I think. That would give the amazing skill talent, at the very least. Probably some extra dots of Merits for a signature fighting style (noting that they're only up to five dots worth of &quot;moves&quot; rather than whole Martial Arts Charm trees, but still signature moves for the character)<br /> <br /> I think I could do something (in my mind) similar in D20 by using one of the variant rules meant for tiny parties: Every level-up, you gain levels in two classes, taking the better skills, saves, HP, and BAB between the two, plus the special powers of both class levels. <br /> <br /> I think I could do something (in my mind) similar in D6 by giving extra starting skills dice/pips, one or two supernatural attribute dice for free, and a house rule that selected skills are half as expensive to level up, chosen per character.<br /> <br /> None of those would be an exact fit, but I think they'd fill the same role, in the contexts of their own universes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T20:52:22-08:00","id":1170850,"title":"","content":"Glorious Solar Saber is pretty iconic.<br /> <br /> Flinty, while I agree with you in general, I do think there are certain specific powers that <i>matter</i> if you're going to port something and keep calling it a Solar. Wyld-Shaping Technique, for instance, isn't just &quot;adaptability and excellence,&quot; it's a crucially thematic part of the Solar kit that they literally <i>enlarge the world</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T20:56:28-08:00","id":1170852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170797-what-are-the-iconic-solar-effects?p=1170848#post1170848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think adaptability is particularly Solar. They're not bad at being adaptable, but Lunars are the masters of adaptation.<br /> <br /> I'd say that Solars are the best at a finite range of skills, at which they shine brighter than any other. Which skills those are vary from Solar to Solar, but probably some two to five Abilities would become a particular Solar's domain of excellence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're both right. The trick is that Solars as a group cover the widest thematic ground of all the Exalted, but that any individual Solar is only one specific representation of that excellence (with some wriggle room depending on how they're built, of course.) Whereas Lunars have a narrower, more specific scope in terms of what a Lunar can be, but individual Lunars have much more flexibility.<br /> <br /> That's speaking in generalities. But in general the Solars are intended to serve a wide range of purposes for people who just want to play one of the Exalted, whereas other splats tend to offer a more specific and tailored experience by design. Like, say... &quot;shapeshifter&quot;, which is pretty core to the Lunars, is much more specific than any of the core themes common to all Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T21:14:30-08:00","id":1170855,"title":"","content":"Regarding the distinction Aqullion just drew, here's a great <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar84_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"84\" data-vbnamecard=\"84\">Holden</a> quote:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Let us engage in a thought exercise.<br /> It's the First Age. To settle a bet, Luna and another Luna that she has spun off, gotten drunk with, and started betting against, call all 300 Solars and all 300 Lunars to assemble in a great big god damned field. Around the edge of this field are 600 identical castles, each guarded by well-trained mortal soldiers. At the center of each castle is a MacGuffin.<br /> Each Solar and each Lunar is assigned a different castle. They have one night to sneak into this castle, retrieve the MacGuffin, and sneak back out. In doing so, they may incapacitate no more than three guards and may not cause the general alarm to be raised. Whichever group of Exalts has the most MacGuffins come morning wins.<br /> The Lunars are going to win this contest. They are going to win it <i>easily</i>, because <i>all</i> of them have the wherewithal to make a decent go at this. The Solars who can do it, will do it <i>much more easily,</i> but there are plenty of them who have like Stealth 0, Larceny 0, and whose only option is to head in like Popeye on a Spinach bender.<br /> This does not make them better than Solars. It does not even make them better <i>at stealth infiltration</i> than Solars. It just makes them Lunars.<br /> </span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><br /> </span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T00:36:42-08:00","id":1170873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170797-what-are-the-iconic-solar-effects?p=1170852#post1170852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're both right. The trick is that Solars as a group cover the widest thematic ground of all the Exalted, but that any individual Solar is only one specific representation of that excellence (with some wriggle room depending on how they're built, of course.)</div> </div> </div> </div>More than a little wiggle room, I think, even just going by the number of dots and Charms that they can start with.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whereas Lunars have a narrower, more specific scope in terms of what a Lunar can be, but individual Lunars have much more flexibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWe don't really know yet what individual Lunars can do, unless much more flexibility is resting primarily on the shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> I mean, when you get Vance to talk about Lunars, he doesn't talk about them being flexible, he talks about them being primal and predatory.<br /> <br /> \u200bLunars as they've been presented so far in this Edition are adaptable in the sense that they've got Castes and some other metaphysical quirks that change depending on what their overall status in an Age of the world is, but apart from that...<br /> <br /> Anyway, I find Blazing Solar Bolt to be among selections of what is iconic.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T01:34:32-08:00","id":1170882,"title":"","content":"I don't think &quot;much more flexibility is resting on the shapeshifting&quot; is necessary to make them adaptable, because shapeshifting as is, is extremely adaptable. Most Lunars are at least decent at combat (because they can turn into a big animal that's decent at combat), decent at stealth (because they can turn into small, sneaky animals. Or just turn into an animal because it's a good disguise), and the majority of them are also good at getting around because they can turn into birds.<br /> <br /> I never felt, in 2nd ed, that Lunar charms made my character adaptable. So unless shapeshifting is suddenly much more expensive or difficult or something (which, other than the totem form, I sincerely doubt), they're still going to be more adaptable than Solars, regardless of how their charms work.<br /> <br /> In fact, shapeshifting is going to make them better at combat than it used to, just because the animal stats are much buffer. I used to frequently turn into a bear for combats, and bears just got much better.<br /> <br /> <br /> But anyway.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I find Blazing Solar Bolt to be among selections of what is iconic. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this kind of thing.<br /> <br /> Solars are two main things; 1)superhuman, 2)infused with the power of the sun. There are other lesser themes (like kingship, or the ability to create order out of chaos), but those are the two primary ones.<br /> <br /> The first can easily be represented in a different system by a completely different mechanic. Giving them high base attack, mega-charisma, 80% stats in athletics, whatever is appropriate for the system. A superhero system's rules would likely be fine.<br /> <br /> (It should probably be noted that Exalted is a specific genre, and things like Graceful Crane Stance represent superhuman ability in that genre. So, a system that represents a different genre would give Solars rather different abilities)<br /> <br /> The second is a bit more specific. Things like generating bolts of blazing light isn't just Blazing Solar Bolt. Light-themed effects are found in lots of charms, especially but not exclusively in combat.<br /> So having Solars shoot bolts of light out of their bows/surround their sword in blazing light/surround themselves in light as they power up etc, would be pretty important.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T01:43:21-08:00","id":1170884,"title":"","content":"All of the &quot;Glorious Solar...&quot; charms seem pretty iconic to me, whether we're talking about Archery, Melee, Resistance, what have you. And while I know the splat expresses its martial excellence in various ways, punching one's opponent dozens of yards to leave an impact crater in a building or landscape feature seems very characteristic of Solars, so I'd throw Heaven Thunder Hammer in there too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T02:02:35-08:00","id":1170886,"title":"","content":"There was a big post about Lunars here, which had no place in this thread about iconic Solar stuff.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere are Integrity Charms that ought to be Solar iconic; something about reinforcing their ideals, and something about protecting them from malefic powers. When I first read the Second Edition Charms, the protection against powers stuff was really one of the things that said to me that they're playing the game at a high level, and it's hard to make them play by others' rules. It's not something that is more important than being able to preserve your heroic persona in the face of pressures and persuasions, but it stands out in a world of powerful gods and monsters (although either way Integrity is interesting as something that is both iconic, and fairly subtle; a Solar who is successfully applying their Integrity would not visibly appear to be doing anything at all).<br /> <br /> \u200bWe've gotten some new Integrity powers with the whole fixed centre of the universe meditation thing, and they are impressive, but they're not iconic of Solars in general or the significance of Integrity in particular.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T03:18:37-08:00","id":1170892,"title":"","content":"For me the iconic Solar Charm tree in 3e is Melee. Broadly useful, overwhelmingly strong, able to translate skill with a weapon into a variety of battlefield roles (ranged attack, defense against magical assaults etc). It's power is both raw, potent and refined, but not too esoteric or vague. It's theme is aesthetically connected to the Sun but not to the extent that it means you must play a glowing Sun warrior. <br /> <br /> I think that tells you exactly the kind of thing a Solar should be doing with a weapon aka displaying overwhelming excellence with it, but it isn't... weird? It's not Martial Arts or shapeshifting or anything that draws on an external concept. It's, I am pure skill, elevates by divine power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T04:08:58-08:00","id":1170897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170797-what-are-the-iconic-solar-effects?p=1170848#post1170848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think adaptability is particularly Solar. They're not bad at being adaptable, but Lunars are the masters of adaptation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean that regarding one particular solar, but solars in general. Lunars may be better at survival oriented adaptation, sure. Their shapechanging also gives them certain options in combat (though honestly I wouldn't call them the masters of adaption there). But solars as a whole will fit into whatever nieche of excellence they need to. A solar exalts in a far away village where an ancient first age dam is about to fail and flood the valley? Never fear, three craft charms later it runs smoothly once more! A solar exalts when his wife has been kidnapped by wyld mutants? A few stealth charms later he is smuggling her out of their lair. Or a few meele charms later he kills every single one of them personally. Or a few war charms later he leads the village. Or a fee presence charms....<br /> <br /> The point is that while an individual solar usually focusses heavily on a few areas of expertise, the solar exaltation itself is very very adaptable, empowering the chosen in whatever way seems most appropriate. All lunars are shapechangers and (in 2e anyway) survival experts. They were good combatans and good at other fields that could easily be enhanced with a charmsets emulating animals (Athletics, combat, Perception, etc.). But they sucked (comparativly to solars) when it came to areas that did not fit the nieche of their exaltation, such as social influence (for the most part) or crafting.<br /> <br /> Basically as you yourself put it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170797-what-are-the-iconic-solar-effects?p=1170848#post1170848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that Solars are the best at a finite range of skills, at which they shine brighter than any other. Which skills those are vary from Solar to Solar, but probably some two to five Abilities would become a particular Solar's domain of excellence.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T10:35:05-08:00","id":1170985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170797-what-are-the-iconic-solar-effects?p=1170897#post1170897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't mean that regarding one particular solar, but solars in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Solars in general are less &quot;adaptable&quot; than they are &quot;versatile&quot;, in that any Solar can be good at just about anything. And even if they try to be good at something that doesn't come easily to them, like shapeshifting, they can find a way to become good <i>enough</i> at it, thanks to Solar Circle Sorcery, Martial Arts Mastery effects or Sidereal Martial Arts, or Resonant Evocations with any Artifact.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wouldn't call them the masters of adaption there </div> </div> </div>The Lunar Exalted are exactly the masters of adaptation in combat, because they have the easiest path to having a solution for virtually any situation which could happen in battle.<br /> <br /> The only Exalted who come close to Lunar adaptability are the Alchemical Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, the word is spelled &quot;niche&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T12:07:49-08:00","id":1171020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170797-what-are-the-iconic-solar-effects?p=1170985#post1170985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Solars in general are less &quot;adaptable&quot; than they are &quot;versatile&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. The point is that there really shouldn't be one iconic thing solars do, as they can do virtually anything if they focus on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T16:25:56-08:00","id":1171086,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to throw the whole Core and Miracles of the Solar Exalted book over and call them iconic.<br /> <br /> Because they are <i>Solar Exalted Charms</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21242-charonferryman","name":"CharonFerryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T16:36:49-08:00","id":1171090,"title":"","content":"I would sum up the iconic Solar effects as &quot;superhuman skill + holy fire (because sungod)&quot;. If an ability can be traced back to one of these two descriptors, it should probably be a solar power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T02:02:44-08:00","id":1171179,"title":"","content":"I would argue that iconic Solar abilities can only be determined on a character-by-character basis. For instance, adapting my Eclipse into a different system would necessitate adapting Soul Projection Method too, but that can hardly be considered an iconic effect for Solars in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T06:09:46-08:00","id":1171215,"title":"","content":"Fury Inciting Speech along Dogmatic Contagion Discipline. One solar can get one speech out, and you get a revolution. I think that this, most of all, is why the wyld hunt took priority one on solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T13:19:27-08:00","id":1171326,"title":"","content":"Rather than putting it down to specific effects (and attempting to ignore the more base claims that radiate from this sort of ... Philosophy of entity I guess) I'd say the thematic Solar power are the effects that radiate out of their inherit authority. More than any of the other Exalted, the Solar are what they do, rather than being are who they are. The will to control thing they have sort of radiates out from this idea space. They conquer, they mold, their power increases to the degree it is challenged (esp in 3rd Edition). Glorious Solar Saber indicates this, as does Dogstar Ruminitions, or the channeling Buddha charm from Integrity; their charms shift the focus of the story to being centered around themselves and the (seemingly) inherit power they tune. I think the iconic nature of the Solar is that where other Exalted &quot;flex&quot; the power, the Solar Exalted must &quot;grasp&quot; it, they reach from the self towards the goal they pursue.<br /> <br /> I acknowledge this is a flawed understanding, but it helps me reckon STing my exalted game and who the Solar are as a &quot;group&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T08:10:14-08:00","id":1171534,"title":"","content":"For me, if we were doing away with the assumption that the Solars are the baseline heroes who do anything you want and do it well, and we are repackaging them as something more specific along the lines of other Celestials, then I would focus on: Anti-demon and anti-undead attack and defense abilities, their &quot;Arthurian&quot; (for immediate want of a better term) themes and specifically leadership, charisma, trust and ruling powers (including diplomacy), and then achieving grand magic with specifically utopian and anti-monster and human heroism enhancing Solar themes (while being less exceptional at grand magic which is just as powerful but isn't specifically immediately that helpful for a role as kings of a new golden age for humanity, without some lateral thinking).<br /> <br /> Rather than detail specifics, the most iconic powers should be found under anima powers, then for Charms, under War, Socialize, Presence, Performance, Integrity, Occult and probably more the attack abilities than dodge or resistance.<br /> <br /> Kind of just think super-Paladin wizard kings, without the Arthurian knightly iconography, and think more grand than lawful good.<br /> <br /> If we're looking to keep them broad and default heroes, then go under each ability and pick the tricks that seem the most memorable or which immediately give you the image of &quot;I've definitely seen this in a film / book&quot; before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T18:31:24-08:00","id":1171930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170797-what-are-the-iconic-solar-effects?p=1171020#post1171020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough. The point is that there really shouldn't be one iconic thing solars do, as they can do virtually anything if they focus on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>God-King's Breath Technique<br /> <br /> E2, Integrity 4<br /> <br /> The Solar Exalted are paragons of righteousness in an impure world. This charm allows you to extend your mouth on a stalk and bite people with it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T08:36:36-08:00","id":1172007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170797-what-are-the-iconic-solar-effects?p=1171930#post1171930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> God-King's Breath Technique<br /> <br /> E2, Integrity 4<br /> <br /> The Solar Exalted are paragons of righteousness in an impure world. This charm allows you to extend your mouth on a stalk and bite people with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>One day, some splat needs to finally get that Charm, if only as a joke.<br /> <br /> Liminals, do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T11:52:46-08:00","id":1172035,"title":"","content":"In a lot of ways, Solars are normal protagonists, but with the volume cranked up. Solars do relatively little by charm volume that you can't already sort of do in many other systems, they just do it LOUDER.<br /> <br /> What little they have that is extremely <i>specific </i>to them seems to involve light-theming. Shooting sun lasers, shining with the light of the sun, holy fire, that kind of thing. So if you wannt to make something that evokes the feel of Solars in other games and settings, giving them mechanics to do the normal mechanical things in the system but BIGGER and BETTER, and also go around being all radiant as shit will get the feel across decently well with relatively small mechanical difficulty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T12:15:45-08:00","id":1172045,"title":"","content":"Cool discussion! It's really interesting to read.<br /> <br /> However, I feel like there's some confusion on what I mean by &quot;iconic effects&quot;. For example, there's little doubt that the Solar theme of excellence is an overarching one and that, for example, a melee-focused Solar fulfils that theme if her Charms allow her to be really good at swording things. However, to achieve that, there's still a few specific effects that Solars typically have at their disposal. For instance, in order to block an attack, you often don't specifically need a perfect defense. Having a high enough defense will, in most cases, serve just as good and therefore support the Solar excellence theme. However, if there was a Solar Charmset printed that didn't include Heavenly Guardian Defense, that would make them feel just a little different, right? No longer can a melee-focused character go into battle with their player <i>knowing</i> that, if they need to, they can turn away <i>any</i> attack. If the exclusion of an effect would change the the &quot;feeling&quot; of the Solars to the point where they start feeling different as a Host, that's when I'd call the effect iconic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T14:51:28-08:00","id":1172077,"title":"","content":"For this exercise, I considered &quot;iconic&quot; to mean &quot;memetic&quot;. Any Charm that people constantly brought up in spirited conversation was a Charm that had clearly made an impact on people's memories and imaginations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T15:09:09-08:00","id":1172078,"title":"","content":"That's also very close to my intention, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T15:23:35-08:00","id":1172082,"title":"","content":"Lots of people talk of Blazing Solar Bolt, but I find that one so bleh... potent, sure. But bleh. Edge of Morning Sunlight serves the same narrative purpose (sun-blessed swordsman cutting through monsters) much more nicely.<br /> Sandstorm-Wind Attack also fills the &quot;cut at distance&quot; trope better, and you will have the two if you go for BSB. Makes BSB feel really redundant and a bit off-tone.<br /> <br /> My primary complaint is of tone, ultimately. With its prerequisites you cleave through the monsters. With bsb you turn the gap between your weapon and your forehead into a blaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 12-31-2017, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T20:34:04-08:00","id":1172152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170797-what-are-the-iconic-solar-effects?p=1172007#post1172007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One day, some splat needs to finally get that Charm, if only as a joke.<br /> <br /> Liminals, do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the new Niobaran Exalted, who will presumably be very inhuman in their themes and could draw on strange aquatic monsters in a Lovecraftian sort of way. If they go in that direction, tentacles would presumably be something they do.<br /> <br /> (IIRC there's also a new type of Exalt that gives an alternate take on some Lunar themes in the way that Liminals do for Abyssals and Getimian do for Sidereals, although we know nothing about them whatsoever.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid"